CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'rq->cmd_type == REQ_TYPE_FS'
#160: FILE: block/elevator.c:576:
+		if ((rq->cmd_type == REQ_TYPE_FS) ||
+		    (rq->cmd_flags & REQ_SANITIZE)) {

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

CHECK:BIT_MACRO: Prefer using the BIT macro
#208: FILE: include/linux/blk_types.h:191:
+#define REQ_SANITIZE		(1 << __REQ_SANITIZE)

Defines like: 1 << <digit> could be BIT(digit).
The BIT() macro is defined via include/linux/bits.h::

  #define BIT(nr)         (1UL << (nr))

CHECK:AVOID_EXTERNS: extern prototypes should be avoided in .h files
#262: FILE: include/linux/blkdev.h:1049:
+extern int blkdev_issue_sanitize(struct block_device *bdev, gfp_t gfp_mask);

Function prototypes don't need to be declared extern in .h
files.  It's assumed by the compiler and is unnecessary.

